provenance.prompt:
Create an original 1536×1024 transparent RGBA production sprite sheet for JAMVERSE '96: Keeg of the Moonmorel Hex performing a right-facing one-handed WINDMILL dunk. Five equal columns by three equal rows, exactly fifteen separate original complete full-body poses, read row-major. Keep the full figure, complete very tall hat and mushrooms inside each cell with broad transparent gutters. Consistent scale, camera, facing, anatomy and identity. No overlap or cell borders. No background, court, floor, hoop, shadows, effects, text, labels, teammate, opponent or props.

Keeg is a flamboyant adult human man, normal athletic human anatomy, black hair and a neat close black beard, expressive face, extremely tall complete purple witch hat with silver trim and small mushroom ornaments. His outfit is layered lavender/purple/silver Moonmorel Hex athletic clothing with belt, rings and restrained occult patterning; matching purple/silver athletic shoes. Preserve the same face, beard, black hair, normal human limbs, hat height and complete silhouette, mushroom decorations, uniform palette and body proportions in every pose. No robe, cloak, staff, monster features, horns, extra limbs, missing fingers, or changed hat. The game draws the basketball independently: keep every hand empty, never draw any ball, sphere, orb, seam, rim or held object.

This is a WINDMILL dunk with one distinct low circular arm/ball path around the hip and behind the back, then a rising circle above the shoulder and tall hat. It must read differently from a straight power dunk: sweep low, circle behind the torso, bring the hand up around the far side, then finish overhead. Pose 10 (zero-based, eleventh cell) is the only release at simulation tick 21; poses 0–9 carry the invisible ball and poses 11–14 are empty-handed follow-through and recovery. Make all fifteen poses clearly distinct and mechanically connected:
0 balanced approach toward image-right, relaxed hands low;
1 gather and bend knees, empty right hand low at front hip;
2 takeoff begins as right arm starts its wide circular swing down and forward;
3 rise, right hand sweeps low across the front of the right thigh, torso rotates;
4 airborne sweep carries the empty hand around the near hip toward the back;
5 windmill's low point behind the back/hip, elbow extended, hand visibly clear of the body and belt;
6 carry the hand upward around the far side of the torso, shoulder turning naturally;
7 rise under control, hand curls behind shoulder toward the back of the hat, without touching it;
8 powerful ascending circle, right hand reaches above and beside the hat brim with clear spacing;
9 high overhead cock, wrist flexed and empty hand poised just above/right of the complete hat;
10 RELEASE at peak at tick21: right arm reaches high toward the rim with open empty hand after the windmill snap; keep hat and ornaments fully visible and untouched;
11 empty-handed arm continues forward/down through dunk follow-through;
12 descending follow-through, legs tuck naturally, other arm counterbalances;
13 controlled landing with knees flexed, arm lowering;
14 balanced grounded recovery, upright ready stance, both hands empty.

Keep Keeg right-facing in all fifteen poses and looking/travelling toward the rim at image-right. Preserve consistent normal human anatomy and full hat, black hair and close beard. Output exactly one true-transparent sprite sheet with sharp readable silhouettes and clean alpha-zero background; no exterior matte, checkerboard, haze or speckles.
